Let {
abla }^{\lambda } denote the Schur functor labelled by the partition \lambda and let E be the natural representation of {\mathrm{SL}}_{2}\left(\mathbf{C}ight). We make a systematic study of when there is an isomorphism {
abla }^{\lambda }{\mathrm{Sym}}^{\ell }\phantom{ule{-0.166667em}{0ex}}E\cong {
abla }^{\mu }{\mathrm{Sym}}^{m}\phantom{ule{-0.166667em}{0ex}}E of representations of {\mathrm{SL}}_{2}\left(\mathbf{C}ight).
Generalizing earlier results of King and Manivel, we classify all such isomorphisms when \lambda and \mu are conjugate partitions and when one of \lambda or \mu is a rectangle. We give a complete classification when \lambda and \mu each have at most two rows or columns or is a hook partition and a partial classification when \ell =m.
As a corollary of a more general result on Schur functors labelled by skew partitions we also determine all cases when {
abla }^{\lambda }{\mathrm{Sym}}^{\ell }\phantom{ule{-0.166667em}{0ex}}E is irreducible. The methods used are from representation theory and combinatorics; in particular, we make explicit the close connection with MacMahon’s enumeration of plane partitions, and prove a new q-binomial identity in this setting.
